            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "If $n$ is a positive integer, then $2.4^{2 n+1}+3^{3 n+1}$ is divisible by:",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "JiqZt",
              "text": "<br />2",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "7CrTa",
              "text": "<br />7",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "L2pBP",
              "text": "<br />11",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "nPr79",
              "text": "<br />27",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Let $P(n)=2 \\cdot 4^{2 n+1}+3^{3 n+1}$<br />Then $P(1)=2.4^3+3^4=209$, which is divisible by 11 but not divisible by 2,7 or 27 .<br />Further, let $P(k)=2.4^{2 k+1}+3^{3 k+1}$ is divisible by 11 , that is,<br />$2.4^{2 k+1}+3^{3 k+1}=11 q$ for some integer q. Now<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{k}+1) & =2 \\cdot 4^{2 \\mathrm{k}+3}+3^{3 \\mathrm{k}+4} \\\\<br />& =2 \\cdot 4^{2 \\mathrm{k}+1} \\cdot 4^2+3^{3 \\mathrm{k}+1} \\cdot 3^3 \\\\<br />& =16 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 4^{2 \\mathrm{k}+1}+27 \\cdot 3^{3 \\mathrm{k}+1} \\\\<br />& =16 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 4^{2 \\mathrm{k}+1}+(16+11) \\cdot 3^{3 \\mathrm{k}+1} \\\\<br />& =16\\left[2 \\cdot 4^{2 \\mathrm{k}+1}+3^{3 \\mathrm{k}+1}\\right]+11 \\cdot 3^{3 \\mathrm{k}+1} \\\\<br />& =16 \\cdot 11 \\mathrm{q}+11 \\cdot 3^{3 \\mathrm{k}+1} \\\\<br />& =11\\left(16 \\mathrm{q}+3^{3 \\mathrm{k}+1}\\right)=11 \\mathrm{~m}<br />\\end{aligned}$<br />where $m=16 q+3^{3 k+1}$ is another integer.<br />$\\therefore \\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{k}+1)$ is divisible by 11 .",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
