          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "Prabhat wants to invest the total amount of $Rs 15,000$ in saving certificates and national saving bonds. According to rules, he has to invest at least $Rs 2000$ in saving certificates and $Rs 2500$ in national saving bonds. The interest rate is $8 \\%$ on saving certificate and $10 \\%$ on national saving bonds per annum. He invest $Rs$ x in saving certificate and $Rs$ y in national saving bonds. Then the objective function for this problem is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "QYDlj",
              "text": "$0.08 \\mathrm{x}+0.10 \\mathrm{y}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "QUTQh",
              "text": "$\\frac{x}{2000}+\\frac{y}{2500}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "qWrgC",
              "text": "$2000 \\mathrm{x}+2500 \\mathrm{y}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "Fdd00",
              "text": "$\\frac{x}{8}+\\frac{y}{10}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "The function is given by profit function\r\n$$\r\n=x \\cdot \\frac{8}{100}+y \\times \\frac{10}{100}=0.08+0.10 y .\r\n$$",
            "image": null
          },
